r\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb5\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li360\sl-321\sb1\f1\fs28\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 Cylinder\expnd-2\expndtw-9  \expnd0\expndtw0 Head\expnd-2\expndtw-8  \expnd0\expndtw-2 Flow:\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li1079\sl-320\f1\fs28\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 0\expnd5\expndtw26  \expnd0\expndtw0 Single\expnd5\expndtw26  \expnd0\expndtw0 Flow\expnd5\expndtw26  \expnd-1\expndtw-4 Coef\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li1079\sl-321\f1\fs28\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex110 0Flow\expnd1\expndtw3  \expnd-1\expndtw-4 Table\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li359\ri917\sl244\slmult1\sb236\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 The flow capacity of the heads can be described by a combination of the valve area (diameter) and an engineering term called flow coefficient.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 The total flow capacity of the intake port and valve has a substantial impact on performance.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 Precise information for a particular head design is only\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 available from\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 flow tests on a flow bench.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 A flow bench is a device which will maintain a constant\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 pressure drop across the port\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 and measure the amount\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 of air flow the pressure drop produces.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 CFM\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 (Cubic Feet per Minute) flow measurements are usually made with the valve at various lifts.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 From this data and knowing the valve diameter, flow coefficients can be calculated.\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverfl