\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li806\ri427\sl244\slmult1\sb1\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 The Engine Analyzer Pro lets you run most any spark curve you want using the Spark Curve Specs available through the Calculation Conditions menu.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 For the calculations run in the previous section of this example Spark Curve Specs were set to \f7\b1\i1 Program sets spark for best power\f0\b0\i0 .\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 This tells the computer to determine the engine's burn rate and then set a spark advance giving maximum\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 power for this burn rate.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 Very few engines, especially race or boosted, can run optimum\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 spark advance with street octane gas.\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb3\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li806\ri6443\sl244\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 By selecting the \f7\b1\i1 Use Specified Spark Curve \f0\b0\i0 option , the\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 See\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 Specs\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 button\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 becomes\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 enabled.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 Click\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 on\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 this button to open up the Spark Curve Specs Menu where you can customize the spark curve.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 You will notice for the Projected Performance of the stock 302-4V, the Knock Index was highest at lower RPMs.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 This is typical, as most engines are more prone to knock at\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 low RPM.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 However, with boosted engines, the highest Knock Index appears with the highest boost level.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 Therefore, the spark curve you build in the Pro will should have less spark advance at low RPM and RPMs with high boost levels.\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li806\ri6469\sl244\slmult1\sb227\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 The only way to develop a spark curve which reduces\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 Knock\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 Index\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 to\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 a\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 certain\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 level\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 is\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 by\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 "cut\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 and try".\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 Let's take the example of the single turbo.\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li806\ri6454\sl244\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 We'll leave Fuel Octane under Fuel Specs at 87 which can be found at any gas station.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 If you had wanted\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 to\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 design\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 to\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 high\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 octane\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 street\expnd-1\expndtw-4  \expnd0\expndtw0 gas,\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 you\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 could set Fuel Octane to 91-93 before building the spark curve.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 The method would be the same.\par
