\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li806\ri427\sl244\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 To increase pressure on the intake system\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 and reduce pressure on\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 the exhaust\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 system, you must\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 first\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 reduce all\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 flow restrictions to a minimum.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 This includes restrictions like carburetor, muffler, restrictive intake and exhaust runners, and especially restrictive valves and ports.\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb4\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li806\fi-1\ri5713\sl244\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 However, even with \f7\b1\i1 zero \f0\b0\i0 intake and exhaust restriction, volumetric efficiency for a non-supercharged engine could only\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 get\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 as\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 high\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 as\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 100%.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 Many\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 race\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 engines\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 have\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 volumetric efficiencies greater than 100%.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 This is done by taking advantage of the pressure waves which are created in the intake and exhaust runners due to the normal cyclic nature of engine operation.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 See Appendix 3.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 The most competitive\expnd16\expndtw80  \expnd0\expndtw0 race engines are developed by maximizing the effect of these pressure waves by proper sizing of the intake and exhaust runners, cam timing and valve flow for the particular engine displacement and RPM operating range.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 These engines are said to be highly \f7\b1\i1 tuned \f0\b0\i0 and are taking advantage of \f7\b1\i1 tuning\i1  \f0\b0\i0 waves in the intake and exhaust.\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li806\ri388\sl244\slmult1\sb227\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 A\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 useful\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 feature\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 in the\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 Pro is\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 the\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 ability\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 to watch these\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 tuning pressures\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 while\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 calculations\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 are\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 being performed.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 See\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 Section\expnd-1\expndtw-4  \expnd0\expndtw0 3.7, See Engine.\expnd13\expndtw65  \expnd0\expndtw0 Click on Show Tuning Pressures button to produce the screen shown in Figure A.14.\expnd13\expndtw65  \expnd0\expndtw0 As said earlier, you only\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 have to have high pressure on the intake side right before the intake valve closes to get a good increase in volumetric efficiency. The example in Figure A.14 shows a wave in the intake port of over 20 PSI absolute, which is over 5 PSI over atmospheric pressure of approximately 14.7 PSI. That is almost as good as running a supercharger with slightly over 5 PSI of boost!\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb1\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li806\sl240\slmult1\sb1\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 Figures\expnd-1\expndtw-4  \expnd0\expndtw0 A.15\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 -\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 A.17\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 show\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 several\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 examples\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 of\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 Tuning\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 Pressures\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 and\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 Flows\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 screens\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 identifying\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 important\expnd0\expndtw-2  points.\par\sect\sectd\sbkpage\headery725\footery743\margtsxn1100\margbsxn940
